<Base title="Privacy Policy — Trypup" description="How Trypup handles data. The current version stores everything locally on your device." lang="en" alt="/zasady-ochrany/">
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Updated 1 Jun 2026 · Controller: Ondřej Kliment, hello@trypup.life</p>

    <p><strong>The current version of the app stores all data only locally on your device and does not send it to any server.</strong> We collect only what the game needs to function.</p>

    <h2>What data we process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Location (GPS)</strong> — measuring walk route and distance + anti-cheat. Local only. Optional.</li>
      <li><strong>Motion sensors</strong> — verifying the walk is real. Local, not persisted.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications</strong> — locally scheduled care reminders. Optional.</li>
      <li><strong>Photos / camera</strong> — optional dog photo. Local only.</li>
      <li><strong>Apple Health / Google Fit</strong> — optional write of a completed walk. We only write, we don't read.</li>
      <li><strong>Game state</strong> (dog name, breed, stats, progress) — local storage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect your name, email, phone or contacts, and we run no analytics or advertising trackers.</p>

    <h2>Data sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not share your data with anyone. Shelters listed in the app are just links to public websites.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The app is intended for adults considering getting a dog. It is not directed at children under 16.</p>

    <h2>Your rights (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>Data stays on your device, so you have full control. Deleting the app, or using Profile → Tester → "Reset entire app", removes it permanently. Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@trypup.life">hello@trypup.life</a>.</p>

    <h2>Future changes</h2>
    <p>After we add accounts, payments and server notifications we will expand this document and announce material changes in the app.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
